WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.588
It leaves one record, in one
shape, whatever the lane.

2
00:00:03.588 --> 00:00:08.961
A machine fix, a recorded human session
and an automated certificate renewal all

3
00:00:08.961 --> 00:00:13.372
fill the same fields: where it came
from, who owned it, who approved it,

4
00:00:13.372 --> 00:00:17.062
what identity ran it, what ran,
and what the re-read showed.

5
00:00:17.062 --> 00:00:18.100
That's the point.

6
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.190
Nobody assembles evidence
by hand at audit time,

7
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:26.212
and an assessor reads one format whatever
the platform, and checks four things:

8
00:00:26.212 --> 00:00:28.762
a prior approval, a controlled artifact,

9
00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.775
a logged execution and a
result they can re-test.

10
00:00:31.775 --> 00:00:34.837
Even the human session lane
fills the same fields,

11
00:00:34.837 --> 00:00:37.750
just with a recording
where the run log would be.

12
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.920
To make this concrete, let's
walk through some examples.
